commons probe

// #1029 review, finding 2. `lower_tail_expr`'s hoist path was the one of T2.1's
// three hoisting sites with no fixture at all: `emit_block_inner`'s is held by
// 945 and `lower_if`'s by 1017, but every pre-existing golden was byte-identical,
// so this one was untested.
//
// It needs its own slot annotation. In async-tail position an `async function`
// wraps the return value, so `Effect.pure(x)` emits a bare `x` — meaning a branch
// assigns `T` where the `if`'s checked type is `Effect[T]`. Rendering that type
// directly gave `let __r1: Promise[Bool]` against a `boolean` assignment, which
// `tsc --strict` rejects outright. The ternary form never had to care, since
// `return (c ? x : p)` in an `async function` accepts either.
//
// The inner `if` is what reaches this path: `n is PositiveInt` is a refined `is`
// check, which hoists a receiver temp unconditionally (the #945 shape), so the
// inner `if` cannot stay a ternary.

type PositiveInt = Int where Positive

fn classify(c: Bool, n: Int) -> Effect[Bool] {
  if c {
    if n > 0 { Effect.pure(n is PositiveInt) } else { Effect.pure(false) }
  } else {
    Effect.pure(false)
  }
}
